<!--Post: 2022--><!--Time: 1103253689-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2022"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 7:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My theory, at least for the moment, is that BTK is dead, maybe long dead, and a family member or someone close has discovered his stash of souvenirs. This person is getting off while achieving the objective of protecting the identity of the killer by slowly getting rid of the evidence. This &#34;new BTK&#34; has nothing to fear from DNA testing and is probably young enough to move freely without attracting the slightest suspicion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2022-->
<!--Post: 2033--><!--Time: 1103260224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2033"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 9:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock, I arrived at the same theory as you in a post I made earlier tonight in the BTK Letters section under the &#39;Dec. 14 plastic bag letter&#39; thread and as you say maybe long dead. <BR>What if a person or persons came across a trunk or locker or cleaning out an attic or storage facility found a box or two that beonged to the real BTK and it contained a diary or journal detailing the crimes along with crime souviners, photographs and diagrams of the crime scenes. Armed with this knowledge they could launch a multi-phased release of this information and paraphinalia and make it look like this is something only BTK would know and have.  <BR>Perhaps someone came across this, I doubt they could keep it to themselves without telling someone. Maybe originally they wanted to turn it over to the police or dispose of it in fear of being linked as a susupect to the BTK case or was afraid of the media attention so they told a friend first. The friend said hey let&#39;s play a lillte game with Wichita and make them believe BTK has suddenly resurfaced. I think it would take two minds to pull this off properly. Both familiar with BTK from newspaper, television and coverages and internet sources. Familiary with the Zodiac case and others like it they could craft their own puzzles and word games and make it look like it was coming from the real BTK. <BR>You are right in that they would probably be younger and have no fear of DNA testing. Maybe too young to remember the 70&#39;s BTK but old enough to remember the 1986 murder linked to him. That&#39;s why items pertaining to the 1986 case were released first. An internet search of what was written about the crimes before that would be easy. Once the first communication was released in March it opened a floodgate of media attention and website activity that would have further educated them and fueled their desire to continue with their game. <BR>Maybe they somehow got their signals crossed and botched the plastic bag release of the Fox items and that&#39;s why it appears so careless and odd. <BR>Of course if handwriting analysis of any hand written recent communications from 2004 matches conclusively with those of previous known BTK communications would blow this theory out of the water.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2033-->
<!--Post: 2034--><!--Time: 1103260944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2034"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 9:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, I see your earlier post now. Wasn&#39;t trying to steal anyone&#39;s theory. Great minds think alike. Is it known whether or not any of the recent communications are handwritten?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2034-->
<!--Post: 2056--><!--Time: 1103269306-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2056"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 11:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock, We are probably the only two who are thinking this so lets look at the communications. <BR> <BR>Known BTK: 1974- Phone call &amp; letter in library textbook. Letter is typewriiten, no signature. <BR>1977- Phone call. 1978- Index card to Wichita Eagle printed with child&#39;s block printing set. 1978- Letter to KAKE-TV two page single spaced. Fifth generation copy of original. I don&#39;t know if this was typed or written but it contained a sketch of crime scene and that would have been done by hand. 1979- Note found in home of Anna Williams. Written there so probably handwritten. 1979- Note written in block letters delivered by mail to Anna Williams. I don&#39;t know if it was typed or written by hand. Contained sketch, the second such known sketch by BTK and that would have been hand drawn. 1979- Identical note that was deliverd Anna Williams is delivered to KAKE-TV. Copy of note to Anna.   <BR> <BR>Suspected BTK: Letter to Phillip Fager claiming to be from BTK does not take credit for his wife&#39;s murder by expresses admiration for who did it. I don&#39;t know if this was typed or handwritten. <BR> <BR>2004 communications: March- Typed envelope to Wichita Eagle with pictures and drivers license. <BR>April- Handwritten envelope to KSN-TV containing picture. Makes no reference to being from BTK. <BR>May- Envelope to KAKE-TV with 3 pages. Typed chapter 8 with subchapters 1-13, word find puzzle and copies of ID&#39;s. <BR>June- Letter to police detailing Otero murders. I don&#39;t know if it was typed or handwritten. <BR>July- Letter/package found in WSU library. Unknown if typed or handwritten. <BR>September- Four letters sent from California to WSU adressed in script to media and police with photocopies of AP LA Times story and name and phone number of a person on backs of each. Person named denies any knowledge. Unknown if a suspected BTK communication or prankster. <BR>October- Manilla envelope found in UPS drop box with pictures and names. Unknown if typed or handwritten. <BR>November- Police disclose BTK self-profile. Unknown if profile was sent to them typed or handwritten. <BR>December- Plastic bag found in park with typed chapters list from May and three chapters missing that were on the May communication. Nancy Fox drivers license. <BR> <BR>So it looks like there is evidence of handwriting of past communications and the 2004 communications. Does anyone know if handwriting, printing or sketch samples of old and new is the same? If Sherlock and my &#39;current&#39; theories are correct, knowlege of crimes and crime objects are something someone could have discovered that were owned by the real BTK but identical handwritten analysis of old and new communications is something that would belong only to the real BTK and thus conclusively prove that BTK is alive. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2056-->
<!--Post: 2213--><!--Time: 1103417548-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2213"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 18, 2004 - 4:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It is my theory that BTK is alive and well and will be caught very soon.  I am more inclined to believe that he wants to lead everyone involved in the search for him, on one last merry chase to the end, but in the end it will be the error of his ways that he will be caught.  In these days of all the ways we have to trace forensic evidence, even a plastic trash bag can be traced down to the store that sold that particular run, that in turn leads to gathering up the camera videos and bingo he will be caught.  I do not however buy the clues that were released about his age, growing up etc...the reason being is that BTK ain&#39;t that stupid...I also believe that all of his spelling errors in his communications were intentional, and the reason I say that is being based on his phone call to the police, that conversation was precise and to the point, unlike his written communications.  He is a game player and is doling out untrue information to throw everyone off the track...also the Petra, Tina thing...out at WSU there are bricks with names in them...one says Petra and a few bricks away another one says Tina, this was reported on KWCH Channel 12 when they interviewed some people who were doing their own investigations.  So once again I say do not believe anything he says about himself, as it is more than likely bits of information about those of his victims.  Anyway just my two cents worth.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2213-->
<!--Post: 2253--><!--Time: 1103472732-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2253"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 8:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tornado, thanks for joining the fray. You and Johno obviously know the facts of the case much better than I do. This latest &#34;drop&#34; confirms for me that whoever is mailing it in is living right there in Wichita and not driving in to do business. So if it is the killer, alive, that is doing this, he is putting himself at heightening risk of the DNA dragnet. Plus, this guy is apparently so enthusiastic that I don&#39;t see how he could have kept quiet all these years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2253-->
<!--Post: 2261--><!--Time: 1103480825-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lanena<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lanena<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 10:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock:  WPD already has his DNA, so what does it matter if he leaves it again or not?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2261-->
<!--Post: 2311--><!--Time: 1103519150-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2311"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lanena, you need to read the thread.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2311-->
<!--Post: 2314--><!--Time: 1103528806-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2314"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 11:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tornado is correct that these days they can trace a garbage back back to the store that sold it and we have seen examples of that on crime and forensic TV shows. They weren&#39;t that sophisticated in the 1970&#39;s but it is my understanding that they could at least trace it to the manufacturer and apparently they couldn&#39;t trace the BTK plasic bags he used for suffocations to any manufacturer in the world. I would assume those bags remain in evidence and if they have linked them to a specific manufacturer since then they haven&#39;t disclosed that information. <BR>I wonder how they are coming along in finding out the manufacturer of the plastic bag that held the Fox ID and items found in the park or to a store that sold them? If they have I am sure it was a store in Wichita. It has to be a key in bringing them closer to solving the BTK case,<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2314-->
<!--Post: 2340--><!--Time: 1103562834-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2340"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 9:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->But lots of people buy garbage bags, not just serial killers in their sixties. If the theory is correct, and it is someone other than BTK making these drops, then he could have gotten that trash bag from anywhere: his mother&#39;s house, the break room at work, church.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2340-->
<!--Post: 2373--><!--Time: 1103579008-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I personally think that BTK is termonally ill with cancer or something and he is &#34;Reaching out&#39;&#39; before he dies.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2373-->
<!--Post: 2398--><!--Time: 1103593884-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2398"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 5:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe BTK made the drop, my point was that he shops just like the rest of us...and just about anything he could use these days can be traced back to a point of purchase...such as plastic bags, tape, batteries, ink pens...you name it, it can be traced, nothing that is made has the exact same identifing marks on it, everything is different which makes it easy to go to the manufactuer and find out the run number, where it was shipped, then they go to the store where everything these days is tracked by computer, and then they can figure out when certain items were sold and who bought them, that gives them a suspect list and then they investigate the suspects.  Say for instance you went to the grocery store, you used your Dillons discount card and purchased a item from the same lot run they are looking for...then Dillons would tell them who that person was because they know who the discount card belonged to.  Or, if you paid by a debit card, credit card, or check..it can be traced back to the purchaser, thats all I was saying.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2398-->
<!--Post: 2401--><!--Time: 1103600415-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2401"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 7:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tornado, it&#39;s a good point, and whoever is doing it, something like what you are talking about is likely to be their downfall, something seemingly insignificant that jumps up to bite him in the ass. Still, if it&#39;s not BTK they may never be caught. What do you think he was doing all those years? I don&#39;t think it was prison. Anyone who has done a long stretch in the state of Kansas in that period has certainly been thoroughly checked out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2401-->
<!--Post: 2402--><!--Time: 1103602275-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2402"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 8:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, I don&#39;t think he was sitting at home knitting sweaters..lol.  Seriously, I think he has probably committed more murders than what we know about.  Maybe he travels as a living and thought maybe he would kill elsewhere while on the road.  I also wondered if maybe his &#34;trophies&#34; that he is parting with would possibly be in safe deposit box instead of in his home where anyone could accidentally run across them...especially if he is married....but I am leaning towards the theory that he is single, a loner &#40;hermit&#41;, no friends, no family...and if that is the case then maybe when he goes on his road trips he puts his &#34;trophies&#34; in a safety deposit box.  He probably doesn&#39;t spend a great deal of money and does his own cooking.  I also think that when he has to deal with people he does so with his head in a tilted down position for fear of recognition...even though no one knows what he looks like...but its like a sort of guilty type of movement on his part that would be automatic...similar to when you discipline a child is the best way I can describe it; anyway just my thoughts.  How do you think he lives and acts?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2402-->
<!--Post: 2405--><!--Time: 1103603954-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2405"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 8:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, you know from the thread that my hunch is he&#39;s dead. But what do I know I&#39;m in North Carolina! Maybe I like having a theory that no one else &#40;except for Johno&#41; lends any credence. I don&#39;t see how this guy kept quiet for almost twenty years, not with the way he&#39;s going now. I think he died after &#39;86 and someone else, not a killer but likely a relative, discovered his treasure chest a couple of years ago and couldn&#39;t resist playing a game. That person would be bursting at the seams on a power trip and far more likely to give himself away than the real BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2405-->
<!--Post: 2411--><!--Time: 1103611331-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2411"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 10:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Live or dead there are four scenarieos. 1- BTK is alive. 2- BTK is dead and an accomplice or confidant is perpetuating the name. 3- BTK is dead and a relative has discovered his secret and is perpetuating his name. 4- BTK is dead and someone has stumbled upon his belongings and is perpetuating his name. <BR>Unlike Sherlock&#39;s variation of our theory I don&#39;t think it could be a relative. Even the Unabomber&#39;s own brother turned him in when he put two and two together. My theory is someone discovered his belongings.  <BR>Both Sherlock and myself agree that if indeed it is someone other than BTK releasing this information and sending communications they are probably a younger person. In their 20&#39;s maybe and having kicks. They would also have to have access to some kind of journal that BTK kept detailing his crimes and how he communicated with police so that now it would appear like the real BTK is alive with information that only he would know and secret signals.  <BR>I think if BTK were alive today he would be between 55 and 60 years old and was probably from Wichita and graduated from a Wichita area high school sometime from 1962 to 1967. Those schools would be either Wichita North, Wichita South, Wichita West, Wichita East, Wichita Southeast or Chaplain Kapaun Memorial Catholic High. All in existence during those years. <BR>File this under the odd things we come across when researching BTK angles: Witchita North had a succession of three principals named O.E. Bonecutter 1941-1945, C.E. Strange 1945-1968 and John Gasper 1968-77. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2411-->
<!--Post: 2550--><!--Time: 1103780650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2550"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 22, 2004 - 9:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK had to be doing something for those 18 years before he resurfaced. It doesn&#39;t figure that he led a quiet normal life while his killing machine, his body, went from youngish to old. What happened? Did he retire and then he needed someway to entertain himself? Anybody can fake being a serial killer. Does anybody really believe there is a real message from BTK in that thread? But what if you somehow got hold of his murder souvenirs? Then you are believable.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2550-->
<!--Post: 2662--><!--Time: 1103891812-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2662"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 4:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Id think that if a family member found his treasure trove they would be horrified at this stuff. Just think, &#34;uncle Bob is BTK!&#34; Id hardly think that that could be contained in any way, let alone enough to play this game. Not to mention most people wouldnt have the audacity to dothis to the familys of the victims.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2662-->
<!--Post: 2670--><!--Time: 1103904158-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2670"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 8:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for joining the discussion, Vdubguy. Good points. But think about it this way: Dysfunction often &#34;runs in the family.&#34; You and I and thankfully most people would be horrified and would not get off on ripping open old wounds. But BTK obviously wasn&#39;t, and maybe someone close to him who was cut from the same cloth wouldn&#39;t be either.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2670-->
<!--Post: 2695--><!--Time: 1103950439-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2695"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 8:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hmmm...interesting...i still tend to think that 2 people arent that similarily dysfunctional...besides, if the survivor came across this stuff theyd be seen as a &#39;hero&#39; for solving this. IMO<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2695-->
<!--Post: 3795--><!--Time: 1105238395-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3795"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 6:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->For all the excitement, there&#39;s still nothing to establish that the killer is alive, only that his trophies are being parceled out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3795-->
<!--Post: 3865--><!--Time: 1105351883-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3865"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->L2829tad<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->L2829tad<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 2:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Agreed Sherlock, <BR>Without Conclusive,Non Exculpitory Proof,&#40;I.E.&#41; <BR>D.N.A.On A Recent&#40;Dated&#41;Publication,&#40;Newspaper- <BR>Magazine,Ect..&#41;&#34;BTK&#34; No Longer Exists..Only his <BR>Trophy&#39;s Do...Great Thinking... <BR>.............THARDU.............<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3865-->
<!--Post: 5378--><!--Time: 1107090716-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5378"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thacket3<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thacket3<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 5:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The recent drops would go a long way to help book sales.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5378-->
<!--Post: 5411--><!--Time: 1107111566-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5411"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There&#39;s a possibility BTK had a protegy...someone younger he told about the crimes...who is following his wishes by communicating this stuff...The fact no BTK like killings have started happening could mean this..or lots of other possibilities..including that BTK might be physically incapacitated..he could be crippled in an accident...or by a disease such as MS...and still be alive and his protegy is dispening this info..as his legacy.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5411-->
<!--Post: 5455--><!--Time: 1107135647-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5455"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nessie2uk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nessie2uk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 5:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that anyone who found/inherited this stuff would go straight to a media lawyer and negotiate interviews and payoffs.  This is million dollar info and it does not seem plausible that anyone other than BTK would play this game.......<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5455-->
<!--Post: 5569--><!--Time: 1107197768-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5569"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 10:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You can&#39;t negotiate the release of evidence for money.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5569-->
<!--Post: 5626--><!--Time: 1107221535-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5626"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 5:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I had a dream last night that he was caught! He messed up while trying to leave something else and someone spotted him and thought he was acting suspicious. It was the wierdest thing-but I think he is alive. I think Sherlock&#39;s theory sounds feasible, but not likley. He is alive and the only thing keeping him this way is this game he&#39;s playing. He is old, but you are never too old to correspond by mail or drop off a cereal box by a pole!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5626-->
<!--Post: 5644--><!--Time: 1107231277-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5644"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 8:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey, has anyone thought about the fact that this may be a NEW Wichita State student? The whole bricks and Petra, Tina thing gets me. Better yet, the bricks at the college may mean he really knew someone&#40; other than the teacher&#41;at the college and his ties to the school are deeper than we thought. How old are those 2 bricks? I remember hearing about a victim&#39;s car that was abandoned on 21st and Woodlawn before. This guy knows WSU and he knows that area well. If you dump a car on 21st and Woodlawn, you can walk right back to campus within a half hour to an hour or take one bus and be right back there. This guy was a student, library aid or proctor to a teacher before at this college. I bet you!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5644-->
<!--Post: 5650--><!--Time: 1107237597-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5650"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 9:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Its highly unlikely the BTK Strangler is dead. A sadistic psychopathic serial murderer is the only candidate for communicating with the police and attempting to taunt and manipulate them for almost a year. The BTK Strangler would never allow others to claim responsibility for his crimes. The crimes symbolize outstanding personal achievement and immense sexual gratification. The unknown subject is careful and meticulous. He would never allow relatives or friends to view his trophies and photographs of victims and the crime scenes.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5650-->
<!--Post: 5651--><!--Time: 1107238447-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5651"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 10:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree he never would allow anyone to view them but what if he died unexpexetedly. A relative or friend could come across them going through his belongings or storage shed or someone unknown to him could discover them in a trunk or box stashed away somewhere. <BR>Unlikely dead? Probably unlikely, just something to think about in explaining the long absense in communications until last year. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5651-->
<!--Post: 5658--><!--Time: 1107259917-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5658"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 4:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hmmm...to elaborate upon what Sherlock said..anybody who found BTK&#39;s info and sought to sell it would be arrested by the police and likely charged with receiving and concealing evidence of a crime, hindering an official police investigation and possibly obstruction of justice...Plus the families of the victims would sue this person as well as anybody who published details of the homicides that BTK committed...so that &#34;million dollars&#34; wouldn&#39;t be there very long..<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5658-->
<!--Post: 5716--><!--Time: 1107300677-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5716"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 3:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK is/was a serial killer. Serial killers kill people. The longer this goes on the more it looks like some sick idiot conducting a scavenger hunt on a grand scale.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5716-->
<!--Post: 5732--><!--Time: 1107308400-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5732"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 5:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with Sherlock. To go from mass murderer to roadside litterer?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5732-->
<!--Post: 5741--><!--Time: 1107315968-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5741"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 7:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m starting to agree w/ Sherlock.  I&#39;m not convinced that turning in &#34;trophies&#34; this late in the game would be enough to get his rocks off.  I hope I&#39;m wrong but I&#39;m really starting to think that someone else is pulling the strings here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5741-->
<!--Post: 5758--><!--Time: 1107353818-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5758"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 6:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re assuming he is physically capable of killing...he may no longer be...Maybe he feels this is his last hurrah...and has a surprise in store for us at the end...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5758-->
<!--Post: 7922--><!--Time: 1108747563-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7922"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 9:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->FBI behavioral-analysis experts it says, not handwriting experts, confirmed the new communications as coming from BTK. No forensic evidence cited. No suggestion that the letters contain information only the killer would know. Without the driver&#39;s license, etc. this guy might be dismissed as a crank.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7922-->
<!--Post: 8214--><!--Time: 1109002157-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8214"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 8:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From a story on foxnews.com&#40;2-21-05&#41;: <BR>Randy Brown, a senior fellow at Wichita State University&#39;s Elliott School of Journalism, was a reporter at the now-defunct Wichita Sun when the weekly paper first broke the story about BTK in the 1970s. <BR> <BR>&#34;This is a very different BTK than the original,&#34; Brown said. &#34;The first letters were full of horrifying details of these crimes, ravings and very graphic information about the victims and the monster in his brain — ugly, nasty, scary, terrible kinds of things that people who saw them still have bad dreams about.&#34; <BR> <BR>Although no recent deaths have been officially linked to BTK since he resurfaced last year, the case has received worldwide attention. <BR> <BR>&#34;It is hard to believe this is really the same twisted killer that was scaring the heck out of everybody — had a town completely on edge — in the late 1970s and 1980s,&#34; Brown said. <BR>- - - <BR>The article says &#34;BTK takes a different tone.&#34; It comments that the original communications were filled with graphic details while recent communications are more businesslike. Hmmmm? Maybe the more horrible details aren&#39;t being offered because the new BTK doesn&#39;t have them give.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8214-->
<!--Post: 8250--><!--Time: 1109014557-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8250"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I want to be sure I understand the premise on this thread. The argument here is that the FBI, despite having a number of people whose expertise is second to none anywhere in the world in every aspect of the behavioral and forensic sciences, is wrong in authenticating the recent communications as actually being the <i>real</i> BTK&#39;s work because 1&#41; Randy Brown doesn&#39;t think that BTK sounds like the exact same person as 30 years ago, and 2&#41; there has been no proof sufficient for some of us on the board who have no idea what the FBI actually does or does not have from these communications in hand that prove or disprove that the <i>real </i>BTK sent them. The opposing theory is that someone got hold of all of BTK&#39;s most secret and intimately held trophies and possesions, learned his secret authentication sign, sat up with BTK late at night learning many, although granted not all, of the grisly details of each murder, and then decided that BTK&#39;s legacy wasn&#39;t already freaky enough and went to work to expand on it. This theory also acknowledges the <i>obvious </i>fact that no one changes in their priorities, thier use of language and thier style over more than a quarter of a century as they mature and grow in experience, even someone as profoundly warped and mentally ill &#40;and downright evil&#41; as BTK. <BR> <BR>Sorry guys, but I have to go with the folks who have some clue of what they are actually talking about. This <b><i>is </i></b>BTK we are dealing with, not some imposter playing this incredibly complex and dangerous game without a full deck or all of thier dogs on the same leash.  <BR> <BR>If the FBI, KBI, WPD and virtually every competent profiler on the planet, with the <i>possible </i> exception of Pat Brown, who has roughly the same professional qualifications as my 10 year old son, agree that this <b><i>is the real, actual, original BTK</i></b>, then I am going to go with <i>thier </i> assessment rather than the well meaning but completely uninformed theories of us Monday morning quarterbacks, myself included, here and elsewhere in the internet. When they catch BTK in the next few weeks, or at least within the next month, I am sure he will agree that he was the individual doing all of this - and hopefully he will say that right before some of the victim&#39;s family members beat him to death with their shoes. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8250-->
<!--Post: 8262--><!--Time: 1109023358-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8262"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 2:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You sound a little angry. What secret authentication sign are you talking about? Do you know for a fact that there is one? No theory is off the table until this thing is over.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8262-->
<!--Post: 8286--><!--Time: 1109038905-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree almost totally with Dpinva above. I am 99% sure this is the same guy from the past. <BR>However, I have to confess that months ago I had a thought which I can&#39;t completely let go of.  There is ONE scenario that might explain how this could be somebody other than the original btk. <BR>The imposter would have to have full access to btk&#39;s souveniers, maybe writings, and knowledge of who btk was for sure.  The imposter would have to have a valid excuse for not coming forward to the police if they are found out.  The imposter would have to know law enforcement procedures and how to contact the media.  If btk had this material in a safety deposit boxthe imposter would somehow have access to the box after btk&#39;s death. <BR>Now, who would satisfy all these requirements:  an attorney.   <BR>Think about it.  btk hires an attorney, puts him on retainer and hires him to manage his estate after he dies.  He or she then has access to all properties, and due to client-attorney privelege does not have to go to the authrorites. <BR>I am a bit unsure about the last part above.  Can any KS attorneys here help me out?  As an officer of the court would you be bound to release all this information to the police if you were on retainer to btk while alive and/or as executor of his estate? <BR>The final question as to motive.  Why would an attorney do all this?  Why would they orchestrate such a fraud?  Maybe they had aspirations to sell a screenplay, or such. <BR>Thoughts?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8286-->
<!--Post: 8301--><!--Time: 1109042650-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8301"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 7:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><b>Mike,</b> <BR> <BR>That is a possibility <i>if </i>the attorney in question did not know what was in the communications. With the way these are being made, any attorney would have forfeited thier attorney-client protection as soon as they <i>knowingly </i>made the drop of one of these communications which contained evidence of a crime. At that point the attorney is a co-conspirator and an accessory after the fact to at least 8 counts of murder. IF an attorney knowingly and actively participates in a crime, or through thier action &#40;or inaction for that matter&#41; enables a crime to be continued in commisison, they are no longer protected by privilege as they are now an active part of the ongoing criminal act. <BR>I like your reasoning here, but the only way it works is if BTK&#39;s attorney had intructions to drop an envelope in Murdock Park &#40;for example&#41; an such and such a day and time and had no knowledge of its contents or meaning. Clearly that is not the case here. I don&#39;t know of any attorney that would risk being indicted and convicted, and stripped of their law liscence, to assist a serial killer or a dead client.  <BR> <BR>In short, in order for the attorney-client &#40;or doctor-patient or clergy-petinent&#41; priviledge to be sancrosanct, the attorney &#40;or physician or minister/priest/rabbi/imam&#41; must be acting and behaving <i>within the law</i>, and making drops of evidence from a known murder scene would be to continue the conspiracy by obstructing justice by withholding non-protected information. If an attorney &#40;or a minister, somthing that has also been mentioned before&#41; <i>were</i> making these drops, then the attorney has ceased <i>representing </i>the client and begun <i>participating with</i> the client in his crimes, subjecting the attorney to the pains and penalties of all of BTK&#39;s crimes as an accessory. <BR> <BR><b>Sherlock, </b>in response to your previous post, I am not angry &#40;just a little passionate&#41; - I just don&#39;t understand why, in the face of all the evidence to the contrary, people insist on arguing that BTK is not responsible for the last year&#39;s activity. People arguing <i>for </i>the position that it is <i>not </i>BTK use a lack of credible evidence to support the contention that it <i>is not</i> BTK doing this because it hasn&#39;t been proven due to the aforementioned lack of evidence. I would argue the opposite - I have not seen any evidence that would suggest that it is an imposter. The reasonableness of it being BTK is much greater than some imposter doing everything they would have to do to pull a scam like that off. Granted, reasonableness in teh BTK case is always a relative concept, but I just have not seen <i>any </i>evidence that suggests that the last year&#39;s events are anything other than the original killer. &#40;BTW, the authentication sign I was referring to was whatever BTK marks his &#34;communications&#34; with the prove they are genuine. Tom apparently has seen it and told BTK in a post that is was a real letdown, or words to that effect.&#41; I am certainly open to considering the other side - let&#39;s hear your case and see your evidence for it being an imposter. If you convince me I will certainly be the first to admit I was wrong. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8301-->
<!--Post: 8317--><!--Time: 1109052699-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8317"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dpinva, We are not making an argument that BTK is dead but rather having a discussion exploring the possiblities of how if he indeed was dead someone or more than one could impersonate BTK by having accessed his trophies and a detailed journal written by BTK. It could be done. We aren&#39;t saying that we exclusively or conclusively believe he is dead. <BR>  <BR>BTK 1979 - &#34;I&#39;m going to get that newswoman.&#34; <BR>BTK 2005 - &#34;Thank you for your quick response on #7 and #8. Thanks to the news team for their efforts. Sorry about Susan and Jeff&#39;s colds.&#34; <BR>  <BR>The kinder and gentler BTK. <BR> <BR>Dpinva 2/21/05 - &#34;Sorry guys, but I have to go with the folks who have some clue of what they are actually talking about.&#34; <BR>Dpinva 2/21/05 - &#34;I still think that there is at least a reasonable possiblity that BTK and the Zodiac are the same guy, or are somehow intimately connected to each other directly.&#34; <BR> <BR>Folks with a clue of what they are actually talking about.  <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8317-->
<!--Post: 8326--><!--Time: 1109054695-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8326"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He is thirty years older.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8326-->
<!--Post: 8329--><!--Time: 1109056320-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8329"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 11:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s good to explore unusual angles.  That&#39;s what folks like us can do fairly effectively.  But 99.99% of the time, we end up back were we started - and where LE has remained.  Certainly, they debated whether neo-BTK was really BTK, before settling on the most likely scenario - that BTK is A-L-I-V-E.  But there is room aplenty to speculate whether BTK is D-Y-I-N-G, and that&#39;s pretty close to D-E-A-D, so I don&#39;t think anybody is being foolish for considering the unusual.  I seem to recall somebody in WPD even saying they had pretty much thought he was dead until recently. <BR> <BR>Personally, I&#39;m 100% behind the idea that he&#39;s alive - the dead BTK theory actually BOTHERS me.  But I&#39;m not sure why that is.  Part of me says it&#39;s because it flies in the face of both the evidence and the obvious conclusions of LE.  But there&#39;s a part of me that thinks he will have fooled us from the grave if it&#39;s just some college pranksters who found his stash in a nerd-house attic.  I have to admit that I actually WANT it to be BTK - that he didn&#39;t escape us.  Sorry - I think this whole thread just touches a nerve with me &#40;which is why it&#39;s so darn interesting!&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8329-->
<!--Post: 8542--><!--Time: 1109195306-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8542"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 1:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, I am saying he&#39;s dead. Sure it makes the least sense of just about any theory out there. But logic could be what keeps this case from ever being solved. Serial killers are strange, an almost thirty year silence is strange, the police have acted strangely. Should we expect anything other than a strange conclusion? <BR> <BR>Have the police acknowledged the existence of a sign of authentication used in BTK&#39;s correspondence? Maybe Tom Voigt was talking about something else entirely. <BR> <BR>Like Pax56, I want it to be the real guy. I want a dramatic capture. And I want it to be soon so I can read the book when it comes out. <BR> <BR>And lastly, when I read Johno&#39;s last post in this thread I almost fell out of my chair laughing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8542-->
<!--Post: 9356--><!--Time: 1109483441-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 9:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD <BR>I WAS WRONG AND I&#39;M GLAD<!--/Text--></td></tr>
